  "created": "2026-06-19T12:50:53.15Z",
  "description": "A standalone mapper node for FluxFlow: an input in, a mapped output broadcast out, the original input fanned to a Failed port on error. Maps each message with a host-provided expression engine (compiled once). No engine required.",
  "id": "FluxFlow.Components.Mapping",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-19T12:53:33.043Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "h1K6nREdwp6PlZYfzc9GcetQWFMxeR6tiZ3sZHhV4L9T6kryBJNG4oGBdidgmGBrxs1hsx8b47GthJYNtaDaWA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 32423,
  "published": "2026-06-19T12:50:53.15Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt as a single standalone flow.mapper node over the FluxFlow.Nodes kit: input in, mapped result broadcast out, the original input fanned to the Failed port when a mapping throws, failures on the error port — all carrying the message correlation id, diagnostics on the event port. The mapping expression is compiled once at construction via a host-provided IFlowExpressionEngine. The engine factory, module, registration extensions, component types/ports, design-metadata provider, definition-options reader, and the expression-engine/type/context-factory registry layer are removed; the node takes its options, expression engine, optional context factory, and TimeProvider directly and depends only on FluxFlow.Nodes and FluxFlow.Mapping (runs without the engine).",
